<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" elementFormDefault="qualified"><xs:annotation><xs:documentation>
      Operome: OperomeStGBGeneralPart
      Source: StGB consolidated, general provisions (provenance StGB 11, 13, 32, 34, 35; German governs; Sections 13 and 35 authored per the marked-up source)
      The constraint architecture of the corpus. The 13 scope carries the authored master rule (prevention duty plus
      non-commission prohibition); its {ExceptionActApplies} resolves against the 32, 34 and 228 exception scopes,
      limited by the 35 counter-exception ([CounterException]); the 11 scope authors [Relative], [PublicOfficial],
      [Consideration] and [StatutoryContent], consumed corpus-wide by name. Authored text is disclosed as authored
      in each scope's rules and the review document. Evaluative residue (erforderlich, substantial outweighing,
      appropriateness, expected acceptance of danger) compiles as structure and escalates at the margin.
      Supersedes the earlier general-part carrier: 22 and 25 have moved to Excluded; 26 and 27 are Parked pending ruling.
      Runtime caveat: consolidated file, not a proven executable, until the loader's scope-local resolution is tested.
    </xs:documentation><xs:appinfo><PackageMeta><Subject>StGB Consolidated, General Provisions (§11 to §35)</Subject><Verb>comply</Verb><Article>StGB 11, 13, 32, 34, 35</Article><ShortName>OperomeStGBGeneralPart</ShortName></PackageMeta></xs:appinfo></xs:annotation><xs:simpleType name="TristateEnum"><xs:restriction base="xs:string"><xs:enumeration value="true"/><xs:enumeration value="false"/><xs:enumeration value="unknown"/></xs:restriction></xs:simpleType>

